<article class="help-article p-4">
    <header class="help-article-header mb-4">
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined help-article-icon">auto_awesome</span>
        <h1 class="help-article-title">AI Copilot</h1>
        <p class="help-article-lead">
            The AI Copilot lives in the Editor sidebar and can answer questions or make model changes
            using the current project and selected object as context.
        </p>
    </header>

    <h2 class="help-heading">Start a conversation</h2>
    <ol class="help-steps">
        <li><strong>Open the sidebar chat tab</strong> in the Editor.</li>
        <li><strong>Choose a provider and model</strong> from the model picker.</li>
        <li><strong>Ask a question or request a change</strong> in the input field. You can attach images when useful.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2 class="help-heading">Context and tools</h2>
    <p>
        The Copilot receives the current project, model, selected entity, and selected property when they
        are available. Assistant responses may include tool activity, shown as expandable tool groups in
        the conversation.
    </p>

    <div class="help-callout">
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined">history</span>
        <div>
            <strong>Conversations are project-scoped.</strong>
            Use the history menu to switch conversations, start a new one, or remove old conversations.
            A conversation with messages keeps its original provider. You can switch models between turns while continuing the same conversation.
        </div>
    </div>
</article>
